From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: eccci: dpmaif: cast pointers through uintptr_t when logging

Two debug log statements print an address with %08X and cast the pointer
straight to u32:

  ccci_hif_dpmaif.c:465:25: error: cast from pointer to integer of different
      size [-Werror=pointer-to-int-cast]

On arm64 that is a 64-to-32-bit narrowing. The truncation is deliberate - the
format asks for eight hex digits and these are trace lines - so keep the
behaviour exactly and make the narrowing explicit by going through uintptr_t,
rather than demoting the warning class, which is worth keeping fatal.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_dpmaif.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_dpmaif.c
@@ -462,7 +462,7 @@
 	i = 0;
 	while (i < count) {
 		DPMA_DRB_DATA_INFO("%08X(%04d): %016llX %016llX %016llX %016llX %016llX %016llX %016llX %016llX\n",
-			(u32)data_64ptr, (i * 8),
+			(u32)(uintptr_t)data_64ptr, (i * 8),
 			*data_64ptr, *(data_64ptr + 1),
 			*(data_64ptr + 2), *(data_64ptr + 3),
 			*(data_64ptr + 4), *(data_64ptr + 5),
--- a/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_dpmaif.c
+++ b/drivers/misc/mediatek/eccci/hif/ccci_hif_dpmaif.c
@@ -475,7 +475,7 @@
 	if (mod64 > 0) {
 		data_8ptr = (u8 *)data_64ptr;
 
-		DPMA_DRB_DATA_INFO("%08X(%04d):", (u32)data_8ptr, count * 8);
+		DPMA_DRB_DATA_INFO("%08X(%04d):", (u32)(uintptr_t)data_8ptr, count * 8);
 
 		for (i = 0; i < mod64; i++) {
 			if ((i % 8) == 0)
